Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(captions): drop transcription repetition loops;
 split lines by phrase

Root cause #6 of clip1.mp4 (handoff/quality-clip1/ROOT_CAUSE.md): the
transcript repeated "I'm like, I just want to have a war" over loud crowd
audio (a speech-to-text loop), and hard 3-word chunks left orphans.

media/caption_cleanup.py, both default OFF until Luffy approves (Sanji Q15):
- CAPTION_LOOP_FILTER: a 3+ word phrase repeated back-to-back 3+ times is
  captioned once (audio untouched; editor renders with placements exempt).
  Real repeats ("no no no", "go go go") are kept.
- CAPTION_PHRASE_SPLIT: breaks at sentence ends, pauses and commas; a run
  longer than the line limit is balanced so no line is a lone word.
Phase-2 harness turns on all review switches (content cuts, ambient pad,
hi-res probe, caption loop filter, phrase split).

Evidence: handoff/quality-clip1/step5/caption_lines.md - in the clip1
window 126 of 136 transcribed words were the loop; captions now read
"Yes, I'm like, / I just want / to have / a war." once. Render + sheet +
step2-vs-step5 side by side in the same folder.
Tests: test_caption_cleanup 6/6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
